@tradition name-on-the-beam-new
// Playtest 1 (seat T): a new Works hand's name goes on the beam (later rotation arrivals). {first} / {names} = them.
// After shift in the Works bay; the crew gather, they paint, everyone congratulates them, then disband.
== mail
- {first} joins Works today. After shift, stay in the bay a minute: there's a name going on the beam.
== ask
- Stay after shift. {first}'s name goes on the beam.
- New hand on the beam tonight. Come and cheer.
== here
- Big letters, {first}. Make it last.
- That's the same pen we all used.   #warm
- Welcome to Works! You're on the beam now.   #warm
== thanks
- Under the cross beam, the Works crew gather round while {first} paints their name beside everyone else's. Then a cheer, and back to the evening.   #warm
== chatter
- New name on the beam tonight.
- Remember yours going up? I do.   #warm
- More names than beam, soon. Someone get a ladder.   #funny
